# OWNER: Nouran - Organization Structure tests (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request")
# Run in order on fresh sample data (npm run setup-db). Demo password for every sample employee: password123
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Login as HR (Salma) -> 200
# @name hrLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "salma.nabil@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Login as EMPLOYEE (Karim) -> 200, used for the permission test
# @name empLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "karim.said@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### ---------- Departments ----------

### O1 List departments with employee counts -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### O2 Create a department -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Finance", "description": "Budgets and payments" }

### O3 Duplicate name, different letter case -> 409 DEPARTMENT_EXISTS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "engineering" }

### O4 Empty name -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "" }

### O5 Delete a department that still has staff -> 409 DEPARTMENT_NOT_EMPTY
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/departments/DEP-eng
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### O6 Head must belong to the department -> 409 HEAD_NOT_IN_DEPARTMENT
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/departments/DEP-eng
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "headId": "EMP-005" }

### ---------- Roles ----------

### O7 List roles, highest level first -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### O8 Create a role -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Intern", "level": 1 }

### O9 Level outside 1-10 -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Wizard", "level": 99 }

### O10 Delete a role that is still assigned -> 409 ROLE_IN_USE
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/roles/ROL-junior
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### ---------- Role assignment rules ----------

### O11 Role above the manager's role -> 409 ROLE_ABOVE_MANAGER
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/EMP-003/role
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleId": "ROL-ceo" }

### O12 Role not above the team's roles -> 409 ROLE_BELOW_TEAM
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/EMP-001/role
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleId": "ROL-junior" }

### O13 Valid role assignment -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/EMP-003/role
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleId": "ROL-senior" }

### ---------- Org chart ----------

### O14 Whole company chart -> 200, tree from Layla Hassan
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/org-chart
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### O15 One department's chart -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/org-chart?departmentId=DEP-eng
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.token}}

### ---------- Security ----------

### O16 Employee (not HR) tries to create a department -> 403 NOT_ALLOWED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{empLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Secret Team" }

### O17 No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
